I disagree with this point.  If you are correct and you have
positive luck you want to keep, either an uncursed or blessed
luckstone works fine.  If you are incorrect and end up with
negative luck you'll want it to drift back to zero and an
uncursed luckstone will stop that from happening.  Having a
blessed luckstone is a belt-and-suspenders cautionary
approach in case of making an arithmetic error.


